# Flying shapes (the host)

Imports the flying-shapes box and adds a `Pentagon` that implements the published
`Shape` interface. Construction asks the box for a `Game`, then `addShape`s the
pentagon. Target ticks the imported game; field access there is the usual
Target cheat.

## Import

```
[[flyingA]] as flying
```

## Schema

```
Sky = @Game
Pentagon : Shape = Int/x Int/y Int/side Int/dx
```

## Construction

```
[:Sky flying.factory().addShape([:Pentagon 640 90 36 4])]
```

## Methods

```
Pentagon::step = { Int/width |
  nx = (x + dx) % width.
  [:Pentagon nx y side dx]
}
```

## Target Methods

```
Pentagon::draw = { @Graphics/g |
  g.beginFill(10183653).moveTo(x, y).lineTo(x + side, y).lineTo(x + side, y + side).lineTo(x + (side / 2), y + side + (side / 2)).lineTo(x, y + side).lineTo(x, y).endFill()
} -> Void
```

## Target

```
%openfl

%init
var assemblage:Sky;

function init():Void {
    assemblage = SkyAssemblage.factory();
}

%step
function step():Void {
    assemblage.game.time.update();
    var r = assemblage.game.playArea.rect;
    wchntGraphics.clear();
    wchntGraphics.beginFill(0x1a1a2e);
    wchntGraphics.drawRect(r.x, r.y, r.width, r.height);
    wchntGraphics.endFill();
    for (s in assemblage.game.shapes) {
        s.draw(graphics);
    }
}
```
